If a jurisdiction has a PDMP-availability and has a PDMP-access-policy and has a practicable-clinical-practice-setting and a clinician prescribes an opioid-prescription for an acute-pain in the jurisdiction then the clinician should review a state-PDMP-record before the opioid-prescription.
If a jurisdiction has a PDMP-availability and has a PDMP-access-policy and has a practicable-clinical-practice-setting and a clinician prescribes an opioid-prescription for a subacute-pain in the jurisdiction then the clinician should review a state-PDMP-record before the opioid-prescription.
If a jurisdiction has a PDMP-availability and has a PDMP-access-policy and has a practicable-clinical-practice-setting and a clinician prescribes an opioid-prescription for a chronic-pain in the jurisdiction then the clinician should review a state-PDMP-record before the opioid-prescription.
